## Design decisions

- **Feedback lives on the learner's message** (`ConversationMessage.feedback`, set via `attachFeedback`), so the orange lightbulb banner renders directly under the bubble it corrects; `PartnerReply.feedback` is routed there when the reply lands.
- **Anthropic turn constraints**: the greeting call has no user turn and history starts with the assistant greeting, so `ConversationService` inserts synthetic user cue turns (first-message-must-be-user, request-must-end-on-user); harmless for OpenAI-style providers.
- **Graceful parse degradation**: tolerant `extractJSONObject` + tolerant `PartnerReply` decode; unparseable responses fall back to fence-stripped raw text as the reply. Missing pinyin for a Chinese reply is derived locally via `PinyinConverter.convert`; pinyin is force-nilled for English replies (bilingual parity — never native furniture in 中文 UI). Pinyin toolbar toggle only appears when `learningIsChinese`, default on.
- **`SpeechRecognitionService` has a `private init` singleton** (contract said instantiate, but the actual file forbids it) — I follow the existing `LiveSpeechTranslationView` pattern: `@State private var speech = SpeechRecognitionService.shared`, observing `completeTranscript` (no delegate; no existing code conforms to the delegate either). A `micSessionActive` flag plus `micBaseline` prevents stray transcripts and preserves typed text. Mic works on both platforms (service is cross-platform). Pulsing red mic while recording.
- **Store persistence** copies `WordExplanationCacheStore`'s coalesced single-writer atomic off-main file write (2s throttle, `conversations.json` in Application Support).
- **Greeting race guard**: re-entering the chat while the first greeting request is in flight can't produce a duplicate greeting.
- No sheets/popovers are presented, so no `.localizedSurface()` sites were needed. Error banner is dismissible with Retry (re-runs `reply()` on current history without duplicating the user message).

